+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+MAIN-confirmed operation retains its standby and gas-release SET behavior. Initial AutoEngage=2 standby without MAIN history can grant one SET after observing released gas, a fresh press of at least 0.1s, and release with target/dashboard speed at least 30 km/h. Failure requires a new pedal cycle.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+After enabling, update and restart to apply the new Panda profile; verify CRUISE standby on the dash. Require 0.5s of initial valid observation and a trial within 0.1s of release. Gas held at restart must be released and pressed again.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+The initial indication alone cannot start cruise; only stock ON confirms MAIN. Automatic SET uses newly observed CLU11 samples, without 10ms delays or changing speed-matching timing memory. The new Panda profile requires dashboard 30–160km/h and each wheel 25–160km/h. Both wheels at least 30km/h retain the original admission; if either is below 30km/h, both must be within 5km/h of the dashboard. Recompute switch/counter parity for transmitted buttons and validate it in Panda. Observe actual ON for 0.5s; explicit MAIN OFF, brake, CANCEL, invalid inputs and existing pulse/retry bounds remain. Vehicle acceptance requires confirmation.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
